Embeddings understand language deeply: Although embeddings capture statistical patterns of language, they do not understand context or semantics in the human sense. They excel at measuring similarity but can struggle with complex reasoning.
Real-World Applications
Search Engines: Embeddings enable semantic search where user queries are matched with documents based on meaning rather than just keyword overlap.
Recommendation Systems: Items such as movies or products can be recommended based on their embedding proximity.
