    for idx, ch in enumerate(chunks):
        print(f"Chunk {idx+1}: {ch}")
Section 4 — Approach 2: Optimal Solution
The optimal solution follows the same sliding window logic but provides extra checks and a clearer definition for edge cases. The steps are:

Tokenize the input text.
Define the window step as (chunk_size - overlap). Validate that the overlap is less than the chunk size.
Iterate with the index starting at 0, slicing the token list to form chunks.
Handle cases where the remaining tokens are fewer than chunk_size (optionally include them as a smaller chunk).
Time Complexity: O(n) because each token is processed once when slicing.
Space Complexity: O(n/chunk_size) as we store all chunks, which in the worst-case scenario, is O(n) in terms of token storage.

