Consistency: Ensure that metadata fields are structured uniformly across all chunks to simplify filtering and aggregation tasks.
Indexing: When storing in the vector database, use metadata fields that are indexed or searchable for efficient query operations.
Versioning: If your data sources evolve, include version numbers or update timestamps in the metadata to manage changes.
Security: Sanitize metadata fields to prevent injection attacks, especially if metadata comes from user input.
Scalability: Evaluate the storage impact of extensive metadata and optimize the schema for the most commonly queried fields.
